MODIFIED VERSION OF CHAPIDIF (from Vos, Grande: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2025.109657)
Allows to use chapidif without GUI, compute and plot with more freedom.
Model extensions:
  - Added the Born-Ochkur exchange factor for the total ELF
  - Added the ability to define the total ELF as a sum of individual ELFs with different parameters depending on the type of excitation
  - Added integration limits
  - Added a smoothed cutoff function
Modifications can be spotted by searching for the keyword 'MODIF'.

An example of how to use this is available: 'Chapidif_tutorial.py'
It uses the predefined plotting functions: 'plots.py'

Linux installation:
1) Download the tarball
2) Create a python environment:
        python -m venv venv
        source venv/bin/activate
3) Install needed libraries:
        pip install numpy matplotlib PyQt6 nanobind
4) Compile the C++ library:
        cmake -S . -B LinuxLib
        cmake --build LinuxLib
Done!

